    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="1050" n="1036" xml:id="pg1036"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.4061 Motion Pictures/348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-18T18:00:00-04:00">March 18, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>355. Hays Organization has advised the Department of the receipt of a report that
                    the Exchange Commission<anchor n="5" xml:id="d774-f1"/> proposes to reduce the
                    total remittances by American film companies to 2500 U. S. dollars monthly from
                    the present total of approximately 50,000 U. S. dollars. Refer your no. 1982 of
                    January 3, 1944. The organization states that this is a prohibitive figure which
                    if accepted would force the American companies to operate in China at a
                    financial loss. It would be appreciated if you would investigate this matter
                    with a view to assisting the American companies and report by telegraph to the
                    Department concerning it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d774-f1" n="5" xml:id="d774-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably the Chinese Foreign Exchange and Assets Control Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
